e its driver uses.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "t5", "why": "The aim and intensity of the beam are not observed; they are read through the headlamp state, the high beam revealing farther than the low beam. The safe distance is read as the stopping distance at the vehicle's speed under the design deceleration; where even the high beam's reach falls short of it, the rule asks no more than the high beam, the farthest-reaching distribution a vehicle carries.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "At night (env.darkness) a passenger car moves on a roadway at a speed whose stopping distance exceeds the low beam's reveal distance, with its low beam lit; no other road user is in the scene."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, with the high beam lit."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "In clear daylight with a long visibility distance and no sign in the scene, the car moves on the roadway with its low beam lit: none of the times of NRS 484D.100 holds."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but the source does not observe headlamps.", "masked": ["sig.headlamp"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "At night the car moves slowly, its stopping distance within the low beam's reveal distance, with its low beam lit."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "At night the car moves on the roadway with its headlamps off."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "At night the car moves fast with its low beam lit while an oncoming car closes within 500 ft: the requirement of the second node governs, so this one does not apply."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed 