ches an intersection from, does not apply: the words relate the two vehicles' headings on the road, not an approach to an intersection. “within 500 feet” is the surface gap between the two bodies (rel.surface_gap, “distance between the nearest points of two bodies”) at or below the literal 500 ft."}, {"span": "t9", "atoms": ["sig.headlamp"], "derived": [], "justification": "“use a distribution of light, or composite beam, so aimed that the glaring rays are not projected into the eyes of the oncoming driver”: sig.headlamp, “headlamp state ∈ {off, low_beam, high_beam}”. The aim is not observed; the high beam, the uppermost distribution, is read as projecting glaring rays into the oncoming driver's eyes, and the low beam is deemed not to (t10 to t12). Headlamps off use no distribution of light and do not meet the duty to use one."}, {"span": "t10", "atoms": ["sig.headlamp"], "derived": [], "source_spans": ["t11"], "justification": "“The lowermost distribution of light, or composite beam” is the beam the words borrow from NRS 484D.210(2): “There shall be a lowermost distribution of light, or composite beam, so aimed and of sufficient intensity to reveal persons and vehicles at a distance of at least 100 feet ahead; and on a straight, level road under any condition of loading none of the high-intensity portion of the beam shall be directed to strike the eyes of an approaching driver.” It is the low beam of sig.headlamp (“state ∈ {off, low_beam, high_beam}”), which the rule accepts as compliant."}, {"span": "t12", "atoms": ["sig.headlamp"], "derived": [], "justification": "“shall be deemed to avoid glare at all times, regardless of road contour and loading”: where sig.headlamp is low_beam, the duty of t9 is met whatever the road's contour and the vehicle's loading, so neither is read."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [{"span": "t3", "rule": "NRS_484D_100_1", "map": {"x": "x"}, "as": "condition"}, {"span": "t11", "as": "de